## Understanding the Issue

### Problem Description

The script uses eval "export $_entry" to set each KEY=value line as an environment variable, but because $_entry isn't quoted, eval re-reads the line and splits it into separate words at every space, so a value containing a space gets cut off after the first word, and the rest silently fails as an invalid export instead of becoming part of the variable's value.

### Expected Behavior

The full multi-word value should be stored as-is in the environment variable, with no truncation and no silent failure, regardless of spaces in it.

### Current Behavior

The environment variable only ends up holding the first word of the value (everything before the first space), while the rest of the value is silently dropped due to a failed export that errors out to stderr, which the script discards, so no one sees any warning that something went wrong.

### Affected Components

toolchain/bootstrap/modules.sh (specifically the module-loading logic around lines 124-127 that processes KEY=value entries from the toolchain/modules file).


